    "Deputy Speaker Benjamin Kalu and other APC officials in the South-East are promoting the administration's record to secure regional support."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "As the 2027 general elections approach in Nigeria, high-ranking members of the All Progressives Congress (APC) have intensified efforts to consolidate support for President Bola Tinubu. Senate President Godswill Akpabio and Deputy Senate President Barau Jibrin are among the party leaders actively engaging with regional stakeholders and religious figures to advocate for the president's re-election. These efforts involve highlighting federal development initiatives, including the establishment of the South-East Development Commission and various student welfare schemes. Concurrently, party leadership has been tasked with reconciling internal divisions in preparation for the electoral cycle. While official party mobilization continues, opposition figures have publicly questioned the administration's future electoral prospects in specific regions. These regional outreach activities are occurring alongside meetings with diverse groups, including business leaders and community influencers across the country, as the party aims to strengthen its nationwide political base.",
